`candidate.py` written. Summary of the change (behavior-preserving, speed-only):

- **TILE 1024 → 2048**: amortizes per-tile DMA/loop setup and feeds the AIV vector pipeline — the dominant lever for this op (every case is ≥1M elements, so all 72 cores stay saturated at the wider tile; no parallelism starvation, no second variant needed).
- **Factored numerator/denominator** through the shared `a = 2w` and `b = w²`, producing each via one `asc2.where` blend (`num = a + where(cond, one, b)`; `den = num + where(cond, b, one)*2`) instead of four branch tiles held live until a final quotient-select. This cuts peak simultaneous live UB tiles from ~10 to ~6, which is what makes TILE=2048 fit (≈157 KB ≪ 254 KB UB budget at the empirical 1.6× factor).
- **Math bit-identical** to the passing original: same `w = exp(-|x|)` (no positive exp arg, no cancellation), same `num/den` per-branch values, same blend condition. Kept the harness-proven `global_tensor`/`copy_in`/`copy_out` API and `real_shape` tail handling.
- Scalar `where` args avoided (use `asc2.full` tile) to dodge an unverified codegen path; where/compare destinations are 8192 B (≡0 mod 256), clear of the known destination-overrun defect.

